414 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Explaining of the Backend Architecture Diagram)
/E (Explaining of the Backend Architecture Diagram)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
415 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The backend architecture for the Fibiyo E-commerce Marketplace, as illustrated in the diagram, employs a layered design to ensure modularity and maintainability. Client requests are initially handled by the Presentation Layer \(Controllers\), which delegates business operations to the Application Layer \(Services and ServiceImpls\). This layer orchestrates data transformations between DTOs \(for API communication\) and Entities \(domain objects\) using Mappers \(MapStruct\), and interacts with the Domain Layer which defines core business Entities and Enums. The Infrastructure Layer underpins these operations, providing data persistence through Repositories and Specifications, managing security via SecurityComponents \(including Spring Security with JWT for authentication/authorization\), facilitating integration with external services like Stripe and OpenAI through External Adapters & Configs, and centralizing error management with a GlobalExceptionHandler. This structured approach allows for clear separation of concerns, efficient data flow, and robust integration of essential e-commerce functionalities.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
